To configure Serilog to output only the class name without the namespace, you can create a custom enricher that extracts the class name from the source context. Here's an example of how to do that:

1. First, create a custom enricher class:
```csharp
using Serilog.Core;
using Serilog.Events;

public class ClassNameEnricher : ILogEventEnricher
{
    public void Enrich(LogEvent logEvent, ILogEventPropertyFactory propertyFactory)
    {
        if (logEvent.Properties.TryGetValue("SourceContext", out LogEventPropertyValue sourceContextValue) && sourceContextValue is ScalarValue scalarValue)
        {
            string fullClassName = scalarValue.Value.ToString();
            string className = fullClassName.Substring(fullClassName.LastIndexOf('.') + 1).Replace("\"", "");
            logEvent.AddOrUpdateProperty(propertyFactory.CreateProperty("SourceContext", className));
        }
    }
}
```
1. Configure Serilog with the custom enricher:
```csharp
using Serilog;
using Serilog.Events;

class Program
{
    static void Main(string[] args)
    {
        Log.Logger = new LoggerConfiguration()
            .Enrich.With(new ClassNameEnricher())
            .WriteTo.Console(outputTemplate: "{Timestamp:yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm:ss.fff zzz} [{Level:u3}] {SourceContext}: {Message}{NewLine}{Exception}")
            .CreateLogger();

        // Your application code here
    }
}
```
In this example, the `ClassNameEnricher` class extracts the class name from the `SourceContext` property and replaces the original `SourceContext` property with the class name only. The output template is then configured to display the class name using the `{SourceContext}` placeholder.

Now, when you log messages, Serilog will output the class name only instead of the full class name (including namespace).

