Below is an Apex Batch class that meets your business requirements. This batch job will update the status of the Salesforce Cases based on the specified criteria. The class implements the `Database.Batchable<SObject>` interface and includes the necessary methods: `start`, `execute`, and `finish`. The batch size is set to 200 in the example, but you can adjust it as needed.
```java
public class CloseCasesBatch implements Database.Batchable<SObject> {
    public String query;

    public CloseCasesBatch() {
        DateTime thirtyDaysAgo = System.now().addDays(-30);
        query = 'SELECT Id, Status ' +
                'FROM Case ' +
                'WHERE Type = \'Escalation\' ' +
                'AND Status = \'Resolved\' ' +
                'AND LastModifiedDate <= :thirtyDaysAgo ' +
                'AND (Escalation_Reasons__c = \'Distributor Feedback Request\' ' +
                '     OR Escalation_Reasons__c = \'Distributor POD request\') ' +
                'AND Category__c = \'Consumer\' ' +
                'AND Origin = \'Customer Care\'';
    }

    public Database.QueryLocator start(Database.BatchableContext BC) {
        return Database.getQueryLocator(query);
    }

    public void execute(Database.BatchableContext BC, List<SObject> scope) {
        List<Case> casesToUpdate = new List<Case>();

        for (SObject s : scope) {
            Case c = (Case) s;
            c.Status = 'Closed - Complete';
            casesToUpdate.add(c);
        }

        if (!casesToUpdate.isEmpty()) {
            update casesToUpdate;
        }
    }

    public void finish(Database.BatchableContext BC) {
        // Add any additional logic to execute after the batch is finished, if needed.
    }
}
```
