In Jetpack Compose, you can create a disabled button by setting the `enabled` parameter of the `Button` composable to `false`. Here's an example of how to create a disabled button in Jetpack Compose:
```kotlin
import androidx.compose.material.Button
import androidx.compose.material.Text
import androidx.compose.runtime.Composable
import androidx.compose.ui.tooling.preview.Preview

@Composable
fun DisabledButton() {
    Button(onClick = {}, enabled = false) {
        Text(text = "Disabled Button")
    }
}

@Preview
@Composable
fun PreviewDisabledButton() {
    DisabledButton()
}
```
In this example, the `Button` composable is given an empty lambda (`{}`) for the `onClick` function, which means nothing will happen when the button is clicked. The `enabled` parameter is set to `false`, which means the button will appear disabled and not respond to user interaction. The `Text` composable inside the `Button` composable displays the text "Disabled Button".

In Jetpack Compose, you can center a `Text` element vertically in a `Row` by using the `align` modifier along with the `Alignment.CenterVertically` parameter. The height of the `Row` will be determined by the tallest element inside it, which in this case is the `Button`. Here's an example:
```kotlin
import androidx.compose.foundation.layout.Row
import androidx.compose.foundation.layout.padding
import androidx.compose.material.Button
import androidx.compose.material.Text
import androidx.compose.runtime.Composable
import androidx.compose.ui.Alignment
import androidx.compose.ui.Modifier
import androidx.compose.ui.tooling.preview.Preview
import androidx.compose.ui.unit.dp

@Composable
fun CenteredTextWithButton() {
    Row(
        modifier = Modifier.padding(16.dp),
        verticalAlignment = Alignment.CenterVertically
    ) {
        Text(
            text = "Centered Text",
            modifier = Modifier.padding(end = 16.dp)
        )

        Button(onClick = {}) {
            Text("Button")
        }
    }
}

@Preview
@Composable
fun PreviewCenteredTextWithButton() {
    CenteredTextWithButton()
}
```
In this example, the `Row` has a `verticalAlignment` parameter set to `Alignment.CenterVertically`, which centers all its children vertically. The `Text` composable has a padding modifier added to its end (right side) to separate it from the `Button`. The height of the `Row` will be determined by the tallest element, which is the `Button` in this case.

